 10913                                  ; POST 22h. Saves the IVT (1 KB) to DC00:0C25 and 5000:8000 (34h bytes) to 145E, installs the stub at 532B at 5000:8000 and points all 256 vectors at it with CS = 5000h+n (so the stub learns the vector number from CS); unmasks IRQ0 only and waits for a tick (DC00:1459, vector -> 145A), then IRQ8 only with the RTC periodic interrupt (CMOS 0Ah rate 3, 0Bh PIE) and waits (1458, vector -> 145B); restores CMOS 0Ah/0Bh, the IVT and 5000:8000. Result: the interrupt vector numbers the OS uses for IRQ0 and IRQ8.
